# firmware/ is a git-subtree fork of 78/xiaozhi-esp32, brought in whole. Marking it
# vendored tells GitHub Linguist — and the scanners that follow the same convention —
# that it is somebody else's tree carried along, not code written here.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Without it the repository reads as a 3.5 MB C++ project, and a
# scanner walking the whole tree attributes upstream's release tooling to this project:
# firmware/scripts/versions.py uploads builds to Alibaba Cloud OSS and takes
# OSS_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET and VERSIONS_TOKEN. Nothing here calls it, and this repository's
# own CI uses no secrets at all.
firmware/** linguist-vendored

# …except the board, which IS the work. Everything else under firmware/ is an upstream
# file with modifications; this directory is new code.
firmware/main/boards/m5stack/stackchan/** -linguist-vendored
